comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-20T18:37:36.178Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: fresh keyword searches for follow-redirects and both exact GHSA IDs return zero matches; current open and in-progress inventories show no exact owner. Full live records for the closed CodSpeed Axios precursor and security/Scorecard parents distinguish these newly published advisories from completed prior fixes. The issue groups both advisories for one dependency patch and does not reopen the completed precursor."
  "2026-10-20T18:44:57.249Z","harness:codex","Independent negative control: OSV reports exactly GHSA-8r9p-f939-6h3c and GHSA-q3jh-wrc6-jgq8 for1.16.0, and no advisories for1.16.1. The installed dependency graph now resolves1.16.1 under Axios1.20.0 and CodSpeed core5.7.1. Maintained all-dependency audit plus patched bundle/source-map/native-payload verification passes. Added only the patched1.x lower bound; the automatic seven-day cooldown and existing age exceptions are unchanged."
  "2026-10-20T19:18:59.369Z","harness:codex","Source qualification CI39479180880 at86edbdc391fdc0bf987257b24f802890aa63b861 passes the dependency/native-bundle gate plus all source and consumer gates. Downloaded artifacts prove10852 passing tests with3 skips and exact100/100/100/100 coverage. Locked and installed follow-redirects is1.16.1 and the direct OSV query has no advisories for that version. The existing main Scorecard instance still refers to older849dbf005 and is a required post-merge operational check, not a reason to dismiss or suppress the alert."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-20T19:19:00.146Z","harness:codex",A registry audit can lag newly disclosed upstream advisories. Cross-check live Scorecard findings with the authoritative advisory range and OSV package/version evidence; patch the affected resolved component and enforce its minimum version rather than treating a zero audit count as a refutation.
